# Citation metadata for vaibify (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# https://citation-file-format.github.io
#
# `version`, `doi`, and `date-released` are deliberately absent: no
# release has been tagged and no DOI has been minted. Add all three at
# the first tagged release, alongside the DOI Zenodo returns for it.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use vaibify in your research, please cite it using the
  metadata in this file.
title: vaibify
abstract: >-
  Vaibify creates secure, containerized environments for AI-assisted
  data analysis that are driven from a web dashboard, so that coding
  agents can build an analysis pipeline without reaching the
  researcher's host machine. It decomposes a project into pipeline
  steps, runs each step inside an isolated Docker container, tracks
  automated and manual verification of every step and its downstream
  dependencies, and connects the result to GitHub, Overleaf, and
  Zenodo for development, writing, and archiving.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Barnes
    given-names: Rory
    email: rory@astro.washington.edu
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/RoryBarnes/Vaibify"
url: "https://RoryBarnes.github.io/vaibify"
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - reproducible research
  - scientific workflows
  - containers
  - Docker
  - artificial intelligence
  - coding agents
  - verification
  - provenance
  - data science
